{"id":14829,"date":"2023-01-25T14:22:25","date_gmt":"2023-01-25T14:22:25","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/news-media\/delivering-the-best-solutions-to-the-customer-2\/"},"modified":"2023-01-25T18:08:08","modified_gmt":"2023-01-25T18:08:08","slug":"van-dyk-in-2022-from-new-designs-to-startups","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/news-media\/van-dyk-in-2022-from-new-designs-to-startups\/","title":{"rendered":"Van Dyk in 2022: From New Designs to Startups"},"content":{"rendered":"<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\">Catch up on some of the biggest news from Van Dyk in 2022<\/h2>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Startups: Murphy Road Recycling<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14832\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14832\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14832\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/1-Startups-Murphy-Road-Recycling.jpg\" alt=\"Startups Murphy Road Recycling\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/1-Startups-Murphy-Road-Recycling.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/1-Startups-Murphy-Road-Recycling-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14832\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">The largest and most advanced single stream system on the East Coast will have their grand opening in the coming weeks. Murphy Road\u2019s \u201cAll American MRF\u201d seeks to revolutionize recycling for the state of Connecticut.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 25px;\">Startups: Rockland Green<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14833\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14833\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14833\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2-Startups-Rockland-Green.jpg\" alt=\"Startups Rockland Green\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2-Startups-Rockland-Green.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/2-Startups-Rockland-Green-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14833\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">As an historic leader in NYS waste management since 1997, Rockland Green (the designated NYS Waste Management Unit formerly known as the Rockland County Solid Waste Management Authority) has now completely over-hauled and upgraded its entire dual stream MRF with the very latest cutting-edge equipment and technologies including an optical sorting system along with enhancements to the fiber recovery line, fully automated container line, and glass recovery system.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Startups: WM &#8211; the Westside MRF<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14834\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14834\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14834\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/3-Startups-WM-The-Westside-MRF.jpg\" alt=\"Startups WM The Westside MRF\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/3-Startups-WM-The-Westside-MRF.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/3-Startups-WM-The-Westside-MRF-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14834\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">WM\u2019s newest MRF in their hometown headquarters of Houston, TX delivers amazing results producing clean paper and maximum recovery of all recyclables using fewer human sorters and a fully automated container line.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Current Installations: Atlantic Coast Fibers<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14835\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14835\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14835\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/4-Current-Installations-Atlantic-Coast-Fibers.jpg\" alt=\"Current Installations Atlantic Coast Fibers\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/4-Current-Installations-Atlantic-Coast-Fibers.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/4-Current-Installations-Atlantic-Coast-Fibers-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14835\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Installation has begun in Passaic, NJ on this dual stream system with a highly automated container line. The paper line will alternate shifts of mixed paper and single stream and include screens and opticals for cleaning up fiber and targeting cardboard.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Current Installations: Westrock<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14836\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14836\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14836\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/5-Current-Installations-Westrock.jpg\" alt=\"Current Installations Westrock\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/5-Current-Installations-Westrock.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/5-Current-Installations-Westrock-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14836\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">WestRock\u2019s various fiber line upgrades in Portland, Louisville, and Chattanooga will clean up paper to reduce contamination and reach less than 2% prohibitives.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Upcoming Installations: FCC Environmental Services<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14837\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14837\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-14837 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/6-Upcoming-Installations-FCC-Environmental-Services.jpg\" alt=\"Upcoming Installations: FCC Environmental Services\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/6-Upcoming-Installations-FCC-Environmental-Services.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/6-Upcoming-Installations-FCC-Environmental-Services-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14837\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Van Dyk is proud to continue their partnership with FCC Environmental Services. FCC\u2019s newest project will be a state-of-the-art MSW + C&amp;D MRF in Placer County, California.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Upcoming Installations: G\u00fcnther Splitter Screen<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14838\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14838\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-14838 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/7-Upcoming-Installations-Gunther-SPLITTER2.jpg\" alt=\"Upcoming Installations: G\u00fcnther Splitter Screen\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\"><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14838\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">The first SPLITTER screen will go into a 35tph single stream system in Illinois to do initial sizing at presort. The system will also feature a full container line with 11 optical units from Pellenc ST.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Upcoming Installations: Freepoint Eco-Systems<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14839\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14839\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-14839 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/8-Upcoming-Installations-Freepoint-EcoSystems.jpg\" alt=\"Upcoming Installations: Freepoint Eco-Systems\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/8-Upcoming-Installations-Freepoint-EcoSystems.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/8-Upcoming-Installations-Freepoint-EcoSystems-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14839\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Freepoint Eco-Systems is partnering with Van Dyk to develop a large mixed plastics pre-processing plant in Hebron, Ohio that will use elliptical separation and positive sorting to recover plastics from MRF residue.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Upcoming Installations: All American Recycling<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14840\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14840\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14840\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/9-Upcoming-Installations-All-American-Recycling.jpg\" alt=\"Upcoming Installations: All American Recycling\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/9-Upcoming-Installations-All-American-Recycling.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/9-Upcoming-Installations-All-American-Recycling-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14840\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">An upgrade of this residential\/commercial MRF in Jersey City, New Jersey, will include Lubo nonwrapping 440 Screens, several of the newest generation TOMRA Autosort Five optical sorters, a Bakker inline overbelt magnet and an eddy current separator.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">High-Volume Fiber Baling<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14841\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14841\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14841\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/10-High-Volume-Fiber-Baling.jpg\" alt=\"High-Volume Fiber Baling\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/10-High-Volume-Fiber-Baling.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/10-High-Volume-Fiber-Baling-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14841\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Van Dyk is proud to supply Bollegraaf balers to commercial recyclers who need the highest capacity and highest speed available on the market. 2022 customers include Pioneer Paper Stock, Quincy Recycle, Taylor Recycling, Reliable Paper, TFC Recycling, Colgate Paper Stock Co, and Interstate Waste Services.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Switching To Bollegraaf<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14843\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14843\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14843\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/12-Switching-to-Bollegraaf.jpg\" alt=\"Switching To Bollegraaf\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/12-Switching-to-Bollegraaf.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/12-Switching-to-Bollegraaf-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14843\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Processors switch to Bollegraaf balers when they need a fast, reliable baler that can handle all fiber and containers. The Bollegraaf factory has been busy building balers for customers such as Balcones in Austin, TX, the Lee County MRF in Fort Myers, FL, WM in Nashville, TN, and Athens Clarke County MRF in Athens, GA.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">Plastics Projects<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14842\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14842\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14842\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/11-Plastics-Projects.jpg\" alt=\"VDRS Plastics Projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/11-Plastics-Projects.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/11-Plastics-Projects-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14842\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Van Dyk has closed deals with Revolution Plastics and others to supply the latest optical technology from TOMRA and Pellenc ST. One project will produce a film processing system using shredders, magnets, elliptical separation and optical sorting to produce clean LDPE film pack.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">E-Scrap Projects<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14844\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14844\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14844\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/13-E-scrap-Projects.jpg\" alt=\"VDRS E-Scrap Projects\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/13-E-scrap-Projects.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/13-E-scrap-Projects-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14844\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Van Dyk is currently supplying and installing AUTOSORT FINES units for the e-scrap processor Colt Recycling, among others. AUTOSORT FINES uses four technologies (near infrared, camera, hi-res metal sensors, and artificial intelligence) to improve all potential end products in e-scrap operations.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">MRF of the Year<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14845\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14845\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14845\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/14-MRF-of-the-Year.jpg\" alt=\"MRF of the Year - VDRS\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/14-MRF-of-the-Year.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/14-MRF-of-the-Year-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14845\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">GFL\u2019s Toronto location wins the NWRA award for Recycling Facility of the Year for continually investing in the most advanced MRF technology available. Five out of the last six titles for this award have gone to systems installed and designed by Van Dyk.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">New Additions: Florian van Dijk<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14846\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14846\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14846\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/15-New-Additions-Florian-van-Dijk.jpg\" alt=\"New Additions: Florian van Dijk\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/15-New-Additions-Florian-van-Dijk.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/15-New-Additions-Florian-van-Dijk-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14846\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">President Pieter van Dijk\u2019s son Florian is the newest member of the van Dijk family to join the company. Florian follows his brother Maarten, who has been Operations Manager since 2017, in sustaining the company\u2019s strong future.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">New Additions: Jeff Fountain<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14847\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14847\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14847\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/16-New-Additions-Jeff-Fountain.jpg\" alt=\"New Additions: Jeff Fountain\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/16-New-Additions-Jeff-Fountain.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/16-New-Additions-Jeff-Fountain-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14847\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Jeff Fountain comes to work for Van Dyk after 14 successful years with Pellenc ST. Jeff brings with him extensive knowledge on how to best implement optical technology in various sorting environments.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<div style=\"height: 40px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;margin-bottom: 25px;\">New Additions: Growing Service Team<\/h3>\n<figure id=\"attachment_14848\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-14848\" style=\"width: 700px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-full wp-image-14848\" src=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/17-New-Additions-Growing-Service-Team.jpg\" alt=\"VDRS New Additions: Growing Service Team\" width=\"700\" height=\"394\" srcset=\"https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/17-New-Additions-Growing-Service-Team.jpg 700w, https:\/\/vdrs.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/01\/17-New-Additions-Growing-Service-Team-300x169.jpg 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-14848\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Van Dyk has hired seven new service technicians to their installation and after-sales support team to expand the company\u2019s commitment to customer support. Technicians are stationed all over North America to respond to customer issues with speed and superior knowledge.<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Catch up on some of the biggest news from Van Dyk in 2022 &nbsp; Startups: Murphy Road Recycling &nbsp; Startups: Rockland Green &nbsp; Startups: WM &#8211; the Westside MRF &nbsp; Current Installations: Atlantic Coast Fibers &nbsp; Current Installations: Westrock &nbsp; Upcoming Installations: FCC Environmental Services &nbsp; Upcoming Installations: G\u00fcnther Splitter Screen &nbsp; Upcoming Installations: Freepoint &hellip; <\/p>\n<p class=\"link-more\"><a 